    LLM: 'Game: Quebec Rummy. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Quebec Rummy (Rami QuÃ©bÃ©cois) is a regional variation of Contract Rummy played extensively in French-speaking Canada. It is characterized by its specific sequence of 7 or 11 rounds of 'Contracts' and its unique rules regarding 'Buying' from the discard pile (The 'Pige'). Like other contract variants, players must fulfill exactly what the round calls forâ€”sets or runsâ€”before they can expand their melds. It is a social game often played at family dinners (les grandes tablÃ©es) with multiple decks to accommodate large groups.",
    objective: "Complete the round's contract and be the first to reach zero cards. Lowest aggregate score wins.",
    gameplay: 'Players play 7 or 11 rounds. Each round has a contract (specific sets and runs). Each turn: draw one from stock or buy from discard (La Pige; 2-card penalty), fulfill the round contract then expand melds, discard one card. First to empty hand wins the round; remaining hands are scored. Lowest aggregate score after all rounds wins.',
